ort of truncate  the whole story and have these sort of  bite-sized episodes and sort of taking  some of our favorite moments and  it  of course there's so much more that we  want to put in there but  i feel like we were still able to tell  the story that we wanted to tell in just  the right amount of time  and um  yeah i feel like it's a pretty it it  didn't feel super different to me  sitting at the table or standing behind  the mic with everybody you know we know  these characters so well after all this  time and  it was just fun  it was super fun to be behind a mic and  just knowing that we're putting our  characters onto  into an animated series now  yeah i think we were able to kind of  blast past the  getting to know you phase that a lot of  actors go through with their characters  and i mean yeah i mean that's what it is  yeah you see it all the time and you  hear people talk about it in film and tv  of like oh man i feel like by it  by how many times have you heard by  episode six they really started getting  their stride uh and it is because you go  through this period of trying to really  figure out who these people were but  since we'd already been playing these  characters for hundreds of hours for  several years we were really able to  just jump in and know exactly who they  were and what we wanted to portray with  them  you mentioned having to sort of  uh  take pieces of the larger  unit from the from the stream but was  there anything you wanted to add that  wasn't in the streams uh whether it's  from characterization just story moments  anything at all  there's always a number of small moments  that aren't you know pertinent to the  main story that you would love to have  seen small interactions things that uh  they're just with the cost of animation  and the time that you have don't quite  fit  so  on one hand you're also like well those  moments still exist in the original  stream so you can still enjoy it and how  it first originally came out or 